heet":"E04 Register","cell":"H5","value":58200,"formula":null,"unit":"text","source":"02 Register/Fixed Asset Register - Updated November 6.xlsx","sha256":"c7d022b2941d242f03cb245e0b39d44fba467889c9d85c1b6879f6d8f752ecb4","locator":"Register!H5"},{"sheet":"E10 Fixed Asset Policy","cell":"D10","value":"Depreciate straight-line from the month an asset is placed in service, a full month in that month and through the month it is disposed of, with no salvage value. Lives for assets placed in service from July 1, 2026: heavy equipment 84 months, survey instruments 60 months, site office units 120 months, vehicles 60 months.","formula":null,"unit":"text","source":"07 Policy/HANGS Fixed Asset Policy v2.0.docx","sha256":"cdc6cc38fd94b6c7d0b411577ebc8a093b3b35cf984380c3726eb0514f3bb128","locator":"Clauses FA-1 to FA-7; Appendix A, accounts used for fixed assets, row 10"}]}],"sources":[{"source":"01 Ledger/Preliminary Trial Balance - October 2026.xlsx","locator":"Trial Balance sheet: every account at October 31 before close; GL Detail sheet: 1500, 1510, 1520 and 1590","sha256":"cd99e34028352ddec9efb7b3908b65716f9090d45b972f08ff5e1b6e944dbb80","name":"E01 Trial Balance","originalSheet":"Trial Balance","kind":"tb","moneyColumns":[3,4,5],"percentColumns":[]},{"source":"01 Ledger/Preliminary Trial Balance - October 2026.xlsx","locator":"Trial Balance sheet: every account at October 31 before close; GL Detail sheet: 1500, 1510, 1520 and 1590","sha256":"cd99e34028352ddec9efb7b3908b65716f9090d45b972f08ff5e1b6e944dbb80","name":"E02 GL Detail","originalSheet":"GL Detail","kind":"tb","moneyColumns":[6,7],"percentColumns":[]},{"source":"01 Ledger/October Close Depreciation Entries.xlsx","locator":"Entries sheet: RJ-03 as staged and AJ-02 as proposed by the October close","sha256":"bab59710ac3a83b939721111ff4cae90b8a4d625d9ec893fd792b1d625318d1f","name":"E03 Close Entries","originalSheet":"Entries","kind":"close","moneyColumns":[4,5],"percentColumns":[]},{"source":"02 Register/Fixed Asset Register - Updated November 6.xlsx","locator":"Register sheet: FA-101 to FA-109 as the staff accountant updated it; October Changes sheet: additions, an improvement and a disposal","sha256":"c7d022b2941d242f03cb245e0b39d44fba467889c9d85c1b6879f6d8f752ecb4","name":"E04 Register","originalSheet":"Register","kind":"register","moneyColumns":[7,8,9,10,11,14],"percentColumns":[]},{"source":"02 Register/Fixed Asset Register - Updated November 6.xlsx","locator":"Register sheet: FA-101 to FA-109 as the staff accountant updated it; October Changes sheet: additions, an improvement and a disposal","sha256":"c7d022b2941d242f03cb245e0b39d44fba467889c9d85c1b6879f6d8f752ecb4","name":"E05 October Changes","originalSheet":"October Changes","kind":"register","moneyColumns":[4],"percentColumns":[]},{"source":"03 AP/AP Ledger Lines - October 2026.xlsx","locator":"Lines sheet: the October bills behind each register change, line by line","sha256":"09b31c30e6feed9f8ac35a238b32828693c673e12234eb8bfc6d3a8c579ae2fb","name":"E06 AP Ledger Lines","originalSheet":"Lines","kind":"ap","moneyColumns":[6,9],"percentColumns":[]},{"source":"04 Draft Entry/Draft JE-2610-FA1 - October Capitalizations.xlsx","locator":"Draft Entry sheet: ten lines prepared November 6, not posted","sha256":"ce24e5523351b2d142f15a03d5f59a3e2c08e8ece399ff0e3fe451739dc191ed","name":"E07 Draft JE-2610-FA1","originalSheet":"Draft Entry","kind":"draft","moneyColumns":[3,4],"percentColumns":[]},{"source":"05 Invoices/KRE-2219 Kestrel Ridge Equipment.pdf","locator":"Page 1, read line by line from the PDF text","sha256":"49e049c6585eb631491d7367e23b905ad30a8f72f72ce319ddb4701b3cdaf799","name":"E08 KRE-2219 Invoice","originalSheet":null,"kind":"invoice","moneyColumns":[1]},{"source":"06 Disposals/Bill of Sale FA-105 - October 28.pdf","locator":"Page 1, read line by line from the PDF text","sha256":"fa15d21f76db0737f3d50e4496bc9db1d1bb41b8b581afd0ac2d100158d93c86","name":"E09 Bill of Sale FA-105","originalSheet":null,"kind":"sale","moneyColumns":[1]},{"source":"05 Invoices/KRE-2219 Kestrel Ridge Equipment.pdf","locator":"Page 1","sha256":"49e049c6585eb631491d7367e23b905ad30a8f72f72ce319ddb4701b3cdaf799","name":"INV Page 1","originalSheet":null,"kind":"invoice","moneyColumns":[]},{"source":"06 Disposals/Bill of Sale FA-105 - October 28.pdf","locator":"Page 1","sha256":"fa15d21f76db0737f3d50e4496bc9db1d1bb41b8b581afd0ac2d100158d93c86","name":"SALE Page 1","originalSheet":null,"kind":"sale","moneyColumns":[]},{"source":"07 Policy/HANGS Fixed Asset Policy v2.0.docx","locator":"Clauses FA-1 to FA-7; Appendix A, accounts used for fixed assets","sha256":"cdc6cc38fd94b6c7d0b411577ebc8a093b3b35cf984380c3726eb0514f3bb128","name":"E10 Fixed Asset Policy","originalSheet":null,"kind":"policy","moneyColumns":[]}],"openItems":[{"id":"Repair Capitalized · FA-3","status":"open","amount":"2336.88","explanation":"KRE-2219 for $2,336.88 is on the register as FA-107A, an improvement to the excavator; it is a repair. The invoice describes the work: \"Repair after the hose failure of October 22. Returns the machine to normal operation.\" Its lines replace a failed hydraulic hose and worn bucket teeth. Under FA-3 a repair that restores an asset after a breakdown is expensed; nothing here extends the excavator's life or adds capacity. The bill is already in 6300 Repairs & Maintenance (AP-10423), which is right. Take FA-107A off the register and drop draft line 5 from JE-2610-FA1; no entry is needed."},{"id":"Below the Capitalization Threshold · FA-1","status":"open","amount":"19393.92","explanation":"FA-109, 12 items for $19,393.92, is on the register as one asset; each costs $1,616.16. NOS-5521 bought 12 items at $1,616.16 each with sales tax. FA-1 tests each unit against the $5,000.00 threshold, even when many are bought on one invoice, so none of them is a fixed asset. The bill is already in 6600 Office & Computer Equipment (AP-10417), which is right. Take FA-109 off the register and drop draft line 4; keep the items on the equipment inventory list instead. No entry is needed."},{"id":"Full Cost Not in the Ledger · FA-2, FA-1","status":"open","amount":"27489.56","explanation":"3 of the draft entry's 5 capitalizations are right and are not yet in the ledger, $27,489.56. line 1, KRE-2207 setup, delivery and sales tax, $9,617.00 to 1500; line 2, CPM-0412 delivery, installation and sales tax, $10,796.40 to 1510; line 3, LSI-0930 robotic total station, $7,076.16 to 1500. Each is part of an asset's cost under FA-2 or an asset over the $5,000.00 threshold under FA-1, and each was expensed when the bill was entered. These are the same amounts the AP review found under its full-cost and capitalization checks: post them once, from here or from the AP review. AJ-01 keeps those lines and drops lines 4 and 5."},{"id":"Disposal With No Gain or Loss Entry · FA-5, FA-4","status":"open","amount":"7500.00","explanation":"FA-105 was sold on October 28 for $12,000.00; the ledger still carries it, and no loss was recorded. The bill of sale and the register agree: Tidewater Used Modulars bought the site office trailer, Phase 4 for $12,000.00. GL 1510 still holds its $36,000.00 cost, 1590 its depreciation, and nothing was booked to 7200. Under FA-4 it is depreciated through October, so accumulated depreciation at sale is $16,500.00 ($16,200.00 to September 30 plus $300.00 for October, already in RJ-03) and book value is $19,500.00. Against the $12,000.00 price that is a $7,500.00 loss. AJ-02 removes the cost and depreciation, records the proceeds as a receivable (payment was due within 10 days of pickup, after October 31) and books the loss under FA-5."},{"id":"Depreciation on the Corrected Register · FA-4","status":"open","amount":"322.39","explanation":"October depreciation on the corrected register is $4,854.54; the close's entries carry $4,532.15. Every asset recomputes straight-line from its cost and life, a full month in October for those placed in service in October and for the trailer sold in October (FA-4). The register's own October column says $5,421.08, because it still depreciates the two items struck above. The close staged RJ-03 for $3,716.67 and proposed AJ-02 for $815.48 on the excavator at its booked cost. The rest, $322.39, is October's depreciation on the full cost AJ-01 capitalizes. AJ-03 books it; if AJ-01 is not approved, this entry falls away with it."}],"incomplete":true,"research":null}